Title: Wafcon 2024: Nigeria and Algeria reach quarter-finals after draw
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [], 'Description': [{'Description': "Nigeria set up a quarter-final showdown with Zambia at the 2024 Women's Africa Cup of Nations after a 0-0 draw with Algeria secured the Super Falcons top spot in Group B.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 146}}, {'Description': 'The result in Casablanca also meant the North Africans progressed to the last eight, where they will face the second-placed finisher in Group C.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 120}}, {'Description': 'Elsewhere, Botswana came from behind to beat Tunisia 2-1 and boost their chances of going through as one of the two best-ranked third-placed sides.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 120}}, {'Description': "Yesmin Khanchouch's 12th-minute effort put the Carthage Eagles ahead before Lesego Radiakanyo equalised midway through the second half.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 114}}, {'Description': 'Both teams would have been eliminated by a 1-1 draw and it was Botswana who grabbed a dramatic winner in the fifth minute of stoppage time through Gaonyadiwe Ontlametse.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 149}}, {'Description': "Sunday's results mean defending champions South Africa and Mali are both assured of a place in the quarter-finals before Group C culminates on Monday (19:00 GMT).", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 148}}, {'Description': 'Banyana Banyana face the West Africans in Oujda, while Ghana take on Tanzania in Berkane with both of those sides needing to win to progress.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 141}}, {'Description': 'The match ended with Nigeria pressing for a late winner, with Echegini sending a curling effort just wide in the 89th minute.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 107}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Chiamaka Nnadozie in action for Nigeria'}]}
